@*
    Circuit-independent favourite toggle.

    Two buttons rather than one, because the offline contract is deliberately ABSOLUTE:
    a button carries the state it wants (`data-bw-favorite`), never "flip it". With the
    circuit down Blazor cannot re-render the button to invert that attribute, so a single
    button could only ever be pushed one way — and tapping it twice would have to either
    do nothing or (with a toggle) end up inverted.

    Instead both directions are always in the DOM and CSS picks which one is visible from
    the `bw-opt-on` class on the wrapper. offline-actions.js adds that class (data-bw-on)
    for the "add" button and removes it (data-bw-off) for the "remove" button, so the pair
    toggles correctly offline while every queued entry stays an absolute value. Blazor
    rewrites the wrapper's class from server truth on the next render, so a replay that
    lands differently than expected self-corrects.

    No pip: the button that was clicked hides itself immediately, so the pip would vanish
    with it. The global sync pill reports the pending count instead.
*@

<span id="@WrapId" class="fav-wrap @(IsFavorite ? "bw-opt-on" : string.Empty)">
    <button type="button" class="fav-toggle fav-add" title="Add to favourites"
            aria-label="Add to favourites"
            data-bw-action="favorite" data-bw-boulder="@BoulderId" data-bw-favorite="true"
            data-bw-on="#@WrapId" data-bw-pip="none">&#9734;</button>
    <button type="button" class="fav-toggle fav-remove on" title="Remove from favourites"
            aria-label="Remove from favourites"
            data-bw-action="favorite" data-bw-boulder="@BoulderId" data-bw-favorite="false"
            data-bw-off="#@WrapId" data-bw-pip="none">&#9733;</button>
</span>

@code {
    [Parameter] public Guid BoulderId { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public bool IsFavorite { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The id the optimistic selectors point at. Defaulted so the component works
    /// standalone; override it if two toggles ever share a page.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string WrapId { get; set; } = "bw-fav";
}
